  <h2>Turn a familiar universe into a useful offer</h2>
  <p>A character can attract attention without explaining what is being sold. A professional buyer first needs to connect the universe with a consumption need: a drink, a snack, confectionery or a quick meal. This avoids treating all manga products as one undifferentiated category. Drinks and instant noodles may share a licence while serving different purchases and display locations.</p>
  <p>Start with your customers. A specialist grocer, online store and leisure venue have different purchase journeys and presentation constraints. Before choosing a collection, consider what your customers already buy and how a licensed selection could complement that offer. Testing a new universe does not require replacing an entire section.</p>
  <h2>Read interest signals without assuming guaranteed sales</h2>
  <p>Social conversations, cultural releases and customer requests can help identify interest. They do not automatically predict sales of every reference. A familiar character, shared packaging image or noticeable edition guarantees neither turnover nor margin. Distinguish attention signals from results observed in your own sales channel.</p>
  <p>Record customer questions and requested references, then compare them with a selection available for your market. To understand the offer, explore <a href="{{ path('app_ultrapop.en') }}">ULTRAPOP, the brand developed by LNS Trade</a>. Ultra Ice Tea is part of its drinks range, while Chipsan and Negisan illustrate savoury snacks and instant noodles respectively. These are different ranges rather than interchangeable products.</p>
