  <h2>Keep food information central to the purchase</h2>
  <p>A licence provides a visual universe; it does not replace product information. Check the reference, composition, allergens, storage instructions and dates when buying. Plan how this information will reach your customers in store or online. The <a href="https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/labelling-and-nutrition/food-information-consumers-legislation_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">European Commission describes consumer food information principles</a>. Confirm the precise requirements for the product and destination market.</p>
  <p>Logistics deserve the same attention. Your assortment needs to fit how you receive, store, display and reorder goods. Check minimum quantities, transport costs and lead times in the quotation rather than assuming that two ranges or countries share the same terms. Our <a href="{{ path('app_article_wholesaler.en') }}">guide to choosing a manga drinks wholesaler</a> offers questions to prepare this stage.</p>
